{
	"nodes": [
		{
			"id": "header",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "## Bipolar Disorders\n\nCondition hub for bipolar I and bipolar II: mania, hypomania and the depression-dominant course, how the two types differ, shared features such as rapid cycling and the bipolar spectrum, competing mechanistic hypotheses, and how treatment evidence is organised by phase.\n\n[[Bipolar Disorders Map|Open the domain map]] - snapshot of 2026-09-27; the map's *In this folder* section is the live view.",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 0,
			"width": 2720,
			"height": 170,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar I episodes and course]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nEpisode definitions against the lifetime course, and why acute and long-term questions must be separated in this condition.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Mania]]**\n*condition* - 19 sources\n\nThe episode that defines bipolar I: its features, where DSM and ICD-11 draw the threshold, psychotic features, onset and course, group-level triggers such as sleep loss and antidepressant or stimulant exposure, and class-level evidence for treating acute mania.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t0_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychosis in bipolar disorder]]**\n*condition* - 9 sources\n\nPsychotic features within manic and depressive episodes, mood-congruent and mood-incongruent content, and where DSM-5 draws the boundary with schizoaffective disorder and schizophrenia.",
			"x": 30,
			"y": 932,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g0",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Bipolar I",
			"x": 0,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 888
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Hypomania]]**\n*condition* - 12 sources\n\nThe milder elevated state that, with major depression, defines bipolar II: its criteria, how it differs from mania, why it is under-recognised, and what screening questionnaires such as the HCL-32 and MDQ can and cannot do.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar II disorder]]**\n*condition* - 16 sources\n\nBipolar II, defined by hypomania and major depression: a course dominated by depression, suicide risk comparable with bipolar I, why it is a distinct rather than a milder form, and the differential with unipolar depression and borderline personality disorder.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 670,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 274,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t1_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar II treatment evidence]]**\n*framework* - 10 sources\n\nWhat randomised trials and guidelines show specifically for bipolar II, why much of the evidence is extrapolated from bipolar I, and where the antidepressant question stands.",
			"x": 490,
			"y": 1004,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g1",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Bipolar II",
			"x": 460,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 960
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar depression and mixed features]]**\n*condition* - 7 sources\n\nDepressive episodes in bipolar disorder, mixed presentations, and why they are distinguished from unipolar depression.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 178,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Cyclothymia and the bipolar spectrum]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nCyclothymic disorder and subthreshold bipolar states: definitions, community prevalence, the argument over whether cyclothymia is a distinct or a milder form, and what widening the bipolar spectrum would change.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 598,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t2_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Rapid cycling]]**\n*condition* - 8 sources\n\nRapid cycling as a bipolar course specifier: its definition, prevalence, who it affects, its links with suicide attempts and poor response to mood stabilisers, and the evidence on antidepressants.",
			"x": 950,
			"y": 908,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g2",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Course and features",
			"x": 920,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 864
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Dopamine hypothesis in bipolar disorder]]**\n*theory* - 5 sources\n\nState-dependent dopamine findings, the pharmacological clues that complicate a single-direction account, and the boundary between group evidence and individual inference.",
			"x": 1410,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Circadian and social rhythm hypotheses]]**\n*theory* - 7 sources\n\nThe proposal that rhythm disruption links life events to mood episodes, together with the evidence and its limits.",
			"x": 1410,
			"y": 670,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Inflammation and immune hypotheses in bipolar disorder]]**\n*theory* - 7 sources\n\nImmune markers in bipolar disorder, the inflammation-depression model they borrow from, and the interpretation limits.",
			"x": 1410,
			"y": 932,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t3_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Cellular energy and mitochondrial hypotheses]]**\n*theory* - 8 sources\n\nThe proposal that cellular energy metabolism contributes to bipolar disorder, and what the supporting evidence can bear.",
			"x": 1410,
			"y": 1194,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g3",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Hypotheses",
			"x": 1380,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 1126
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_0",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar genetics and polygenic risk]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nPolygenic architecture in bipolar disorder, genetic sharing with other conditions, and why loci are not mechanisms or diagnoses.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 360,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_1",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar MRI findings and their limits]]**\n*method* - 5 sources\n\nWhat consortium imaging studies show in bipolar disorder, the confounds they cannot remove, and why they do not classify individuals.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 622,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_2",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Phase-specific bipolar treatment evidence]]**\n*framework* - 6 sources\n\nWhy bipolar treatment evidence is organised by phase, how guidelines attach strength to evidence, and the boundaries of what trials measure.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 884,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 226,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_3",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Bipolar psychotherapy evidence]]**\n*framework* - 5 sources\n\nWhat adjunctive psychotherapy trials in bipolar disorder test, what they find for recurrence and symptoms, and why component estimates are averages.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 1170,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_4",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Lithium mechanisms and uncertainty]]**\n*mechanism* - 5 sources\n\nLithium's signalling targets, why its recurrence-prevention mechanism stays unresolved, and how narrow-window monitoring is a class property.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 1432,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_5",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Psychoeducation and social rhythms]]**\n*framework* - 7 sources\n\nPsychoeducation and social rhythm components, the circadian machinery they target, and the status of social zeitgeber theory.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 1694,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 202,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_6",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Mood monitoring and early warning signs in bipolar disorder]]**\n*framework* - 8 sources\n\nEarly warning signs of relapse, self-monitoring and digital phenotyping in bipolar disorder, and what current evidence shows about predicting episodes at group level.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 1956,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "t4_7",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**[[Antidepressants in bipolar disorder]]**\n*framework* - 15 sources\n\nWhy antidepressants are contested in bipolar disorder: switch risk into hypomania or mania, the untested mixed-features case, what acute trials, maintenance evidence and guidelines conclude, and the bipolar II question.",
			"x": 1870,
			"y": 2266,
			"width": 360,
			"height": 250,
			"color": "#F0506E"
		},
		{
			"id": "g4",
			"type": "group",
			"label": "Evidence and treatment",
			"x": 1840,
			"y": 310,
			"width": 420,
			"height": 2246
		},
